<!--
  RM_LeaningScrub_Namers.xml                 LEANINGSCRUB_GPT_ENRICHMENT_1

  Names for the named sweetline trees (Source/RM_SweetlineStation.cs, which calls
  NameGenerator.GenerateName(namer, validator); the root is this pack's first rule
  keyword, r_name, and the engine title-cases the result, leaving "the", "of" and
  similar small words lower case mid-name).

  REGISTER RULED 2026-10-09 (question card): plain English landmark names, the
  way travellers name a tree on a road: "the Silver Mark", "Giants' Waymark",
  "Where the Wind Turned". No coined words. LEANINGSCRUB_SWEETLINE_NAME_REGISTER_1.
  Patterns: [adj] [landmark]; [landmark] of the [walker]; the [adj] [tree];
  Where the [walker] [deed]. The RM tier carries no canon name; keep it so.
  Replace the lists to widen them, keep the defName.
-->
